Small-Business Network Installation & Deployment – Mosaic Café

Location: Old Bridge, NJ
Completed: 2021
Deployment: Three Ubiquiti UniFi access points, wired Ethernet infrastructure, router, network switches, and POS device connectivity.

Project Overview

Planned and completed a network infrastructure installation for Mosaic Café, a restaurant in Old Bridge, NJ. The deployment included establishing wired and wireless network connectivity throughout the building to support point-of-sale (POS) systems, kitchen printers, staff devices, and customer Wi-Fi.

The work involved selecting and positioning network hardware, installing ceiling-mounted wireless access points, routing Ethernet cabling between areas of the building, setting up network switches, integrating POS equipment, and testing wireless coverage and connectivity.

This was a hands-on infrastructure deployment, followed by ongoing troubleshooting and support of the restaurant's network-connected equipment.

Scope of Work

Wireless Infrastructure: Installed three ceiling-mounted Ubiquiti UniFi access points in the kitchen, back room, and dining area to improve wireless coverage throughout the restaurant.

Structured Cabling: Routed Ethernet cabling through the building, including basement cable runs, and used surface-mount raceways for clean, organized cable management.

Network Hardware: Set up the primary router, network switches, power adapters, and supporting hardware to distribute connectivity throughout the building.

POS Integration: Connected and supported front-of-house POS tablets, kitchen printers, and other network-dependent equipment.

Installation & Testing: Mounted access points, established wired connections, tested Wi-Fi coverage, and troubleshot connectivity issues.

Ongoing Technical Support: Served as an on-site technical resource for network, hardware, printer, and device connectivity issues affecting restaurant operations.
